{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$start=1; $end=240; $i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r2\\\\input.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; if ($i -ge $start -and $i -le $end) { '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ } }'","aggregated_output":"   1: # dynamic_story -- Story-Derived Visual Direction: Scoped Design (docs-only)\r\n   2: \r\n   3: Date: 2026-07-12 (rev 2 -- hardened by r1 kibitz: codex gpt-5.6-sol @ ultra +\r\n   4: antigravity gemini-3.5-pro; driver anchor + grounding in\r\n   5: kibitz-runs/2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual/r1/)\r\n   6: Author: Claude (Cowork), docs-only architecture owner for this feature.\r\n   7: Implementation owner: Codex (all code, tests, registries, prompts, workflow JSON).\r\n   8: Status: DESIGN ONLY. Nothing in this document is implemented. No code, test,\r\n   9: prompt, registry, or workflows/otr_canonical.json change accompanies it.\r\n  10: \r\n  11: Scope contract honored here:\r\n  12: \r\n  13: - One additional option (`dynamic_story`) in the EXISTING visual-style dropdown.\r\n  14: - When selected, an LLM reads the final accepted/frozen story and authors an\r\n  15:   episode-specific, evidence-bound `visual_direction` artifact that every\r\n  16:   downstream visual composer consumes.\r\n  17: - An explicit user-selected named visual pack keeps current behavior,\r\n  18:   byte-identical, and always wins. `dynamic_story` is opt-in per episode.\r\n  19: \r\n  20: Every code claim below is grounded `file:line` against the real Windows repo at\r\n  21: the time of writing (v2.0-alpha working tree, 2026-07-12).\r\n  22: \r\n  23: ---\r\n  24: \r\n  25: ## 1. Grounded current dataflow (what exists today)\r\n  26: \r\n  27: ### 1.1 The visual-style selector and its one stamping point\r\n  28: \r\n  29: - The dropdown lives on OTR_LedgerScriptWriter: choices come LIVE from the\r\n  30:   visual-style pack registry (`list_style_ids()`) at INPUT_TYPES\r\n  31:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:2871-2889), default `sci_fi_radio`.\r\n  32: - The id is gated fail-loud at the top of `run()` beside the source-bank gate:\r\n  33:   `_otr_visual_styles.resolve_visual_style(visual_style)` -- unknown id raises\r\n  34:   `UnknownVisualStyleError` before ANY story work\r\n  35:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3334-3339).\r\n  36: - The ONE authoritative stamp: `meta[\"visual_style\"] = resolved[\"visual_style\"]`\r\n  37:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3651-3655). The comment there is the\r\n  38:   threading law: \"every downstream visual composer reads meta['visual_style']\r\n  39:   via get_visual_style(meta) off the serialized ledger\".\r\n  40: - Channel separation is explicit and load-bearing: `meta.style` is the STORY\r\n  41:   grammar slug (from the story contract), `meta.visual_style` is the visual\r\n  42:   prompt-pack selector; the two are never crossed\r\n  43:   (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:216-222, 2249-2261).\r\n  44: \r\n  45: ### 1.2 The pack registry (the resolution seam dynamic_story must enter through)\r\n  46: \r\n  47: - Packs are JSON files under `nodes/visual_styles/<style_id>.json`; the module\r\n  48:   is pure behavior, lazy, fail-loud (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:3-13, 50).\r\n  49: - `DEFAULT_STYLE_ID = \"sci_fi_radio\"` (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:53).\r\n  50: - Schema v2 is a FIXED field inventory: v1 fields (style_id, label, the four\r\n  51:   tails, forbidden_terms, ...) + 11 required look/subject strings + 4 dict\r\n  52:   fields with exact key sets (open_subjects, motion_registers,\r\n  53:   still_word_typography, still_word_backdrop)\r\n  54:   (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:60-102). Validation is strict: template\r\n  55:   placeholder rules, mouth-vocabulary contract, 240-char motion budget,\r\n  56:   forbidden-terms lint (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:109-123, 184+).\r\n  57: - Resolution: `resolve_visual_style(style_id)` -- unknown id = hard error, no\r\n  58:   fallback (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:367-375); `get_visual_style(meta)` --\r\n  59:   absent/empty `meta[\"visual_style\"]` = production default; PRESENT-but-unknown\r\n  60:   fails LOUD (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:378-390). Both are META-ONLY seams --\r\n  61:   they never see `lines`/`cast`/`beats` (r1 finding; drives section 4.3).\r\n  62: - The loaded packs are CACHED module-globally (`_STYLES`,\r\n  63:   nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:170, 355-359). A per-episode dynamic pack must\r\n  64:   NEVER enter that cache (r1 antigravity S3; section 5).\r\n  65: - The geometry-vs-look law (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:7-9): packs own ONLY\r\n  66:   look/subject vocabulary; framing/headroom/mouth-safety GEOMETRY stays in\r\n  67:   Python. `dynamic_story` must obey the same law -- and r1 tightened it\r\n  68:   further: the LLM does not even author every pack LOOK field (section 2.2).\r\n  69: \r\n  70: ### 1.3 The story freeze boundary (what \"final accepted story\" means)\r\n  71: \r\n  72: - OTR_LedgerScriptWriter -> OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade; Phase 10 runs the\r\n  73:   deterministic gap audit and, on success, stamps\r\n  74:   `meta.cleanup_locked = True`, `meta.freeze_timestamp` (ISO-8601 UTC), and\r\n  75:   `meta.freeze_verdict = frozen_clean | frozen_with_warns`\r\n  76:   (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:758-819, stamps at 806-811). Critical gaps raise\r\n  77:   `FreezeAssertionError` and stamp `needs_full_rerun`\r\n  78:   (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:787-795).\r\n  79: - Freeze locks story CONTENT, not the whole rows: post-freeze extension is an\r\n  80:   established pattern. OTR_CastLock assigns voice presets AFTER the freeze\r\n  81:   (acknowledged inside the freeze audit itself,\r\n  82:   nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:493-502); OTR_ShotLock overlays per-line audio\r\n  83:   timing IN PLACE (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:169-221) and stamps a whole\r\n  84:   `ledger['video']` section + `meta.video_revision`\r\n  85:   (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1104-1131). Consequence (r1 must-fix): the RAW\r\n  86:   `lines`/`cast` arrays are NOT stable post-freeze -- any staleness check must\r\n  87:   hash an authored-content PROJECTION, never the raw rows (section 2.3).\r\n  88: - The cascade unloads a locally-resident writer LLM in a `finally` block and\r\n  89:   stamps `meta.freeze_unload_ok` (nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:377-387,\r\n  90:   453-478) -- the VRAM handoff any post-freeze LLM node must reproduce\r\n  91:   (section 4.5).\r\n  92: \r\n  93: ### 1.4 Canonical wiring (workflows/otr_canonical.json, live graph)\r\n  94: \r\n  95: Grounded by walking `nodes[]`/`links[]` of the real file (litegraph schema,\r\n  96: single-line JSON; node ids below are the live ids):\r\n  97: \r\n  98: - Writer (node 1) `script_json` -> link 230 -> FreezeCascade (node 62).\r\n  99:   The writer's `visual_style` widget is combined widget slot 24\r\n 100:   (`widgets_values[24] == \"sci_fi_radio\"` in the canonical file; input name\r\n 101:   `visual_style` at in[24]).\r\n 102: - FreezeCascade out[1] `script_json` -> link 255 -> OTR_MetaBriefImagePromptGen\r\n 103:   (node 89) in[0], and -> link 252 -> OTR_ShotLock (node 90) in[0].\r\n 104: - OTR_VideoDirector (node 87) `video_policy_json` -> link 270 ->\r\n 105:   OTR_ImageDirector (node 88) in[0], and -> link 251 -> ShotLock in[2].\r\n 106: - ImageDirector `image_policy_json` -> link 254 -> MetaBrief in[1], and ->\r\n 107:   link 257 -> OTR_ImageGenDispatcher (node 91) in[1].\r\n 108: - MetaBrief out[0] `image_prompts_json` -> link 258 -> Dispatcher in[2].\r\n 109: - ShotLock out[0] `patched_ledger_json` -> link 256 -> Dispatcher in[0];\r\n 110:   ShotLock out[4] `episode_id` -> link 268 -> Dispatcher in[4].\r\n 111: - OTR_EpisodeAssembler (node 7) out[3] `audio_done` -> link 253 -> ShotLock\r\n 112:   in[1] and -> link 259 -> Dispatcher gate_in.\r\n 113: - Dispatcher out[0] -> link 260 -> OTR_VideoRenderBatch (node 92) in[0];\r\n 114:   Dispatcher out[1] `image_done` -> link 267 -> RenderBatch in[2].\r\n 115: \r\n 116: The frozen ledger fans out on FreezeCascade out[1]; every visual composer sees\r\n 117: `meta.visual_style` on that wire. The Dispatcher receives its ledger via\r\n 118: ShotLock's whole-ledger re-serialization (parse at nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1040,\r\n 119: re-emit at :1142), so a meta artifact stamped upstream reaches it with no\r\n 120: extra wire (r1 anchor A1).\r\n 121: \r\n 122: ### 1.5 Where the style is actually consumed (resolve-once contract)\r\n 123: \r\n 124: - Image prompts: `derive_image_prompts` resolves the style ONCE at entry --\r\n 125:   `_vstyle = _resolve_style(meta)` -- and threads it down; \"an unknown\r\n 126:   meta['visual_style'] stops the episode HERE, before any prompt is composed\"\r\n 127:   (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1601-1609). Consumers of the threaded\r\n 128:   pack include: portrait fallback + LLM instruction builders\r\n 129:   (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1148-1238), beat-aware character scene\r\n 130:   builder (:1241-1366), radio-host prompts (`build_radio_host_prompt`,\r\n 131:   :356-444), mesh fodder + background plate (:1437-1496), still_word cards\r\n 132:   (`compose_still_word_prompt`, :942-1013), and the aspect anchors\r\n 133:   (`_style_anchor_for_aspect`, :171-188).\r\n 134: - Video prompts: ShotLock's M4 creative derivation finishes every talking-head\r\n 135:   prompt through `finish_visual_prompt(meta, text_prompt)` -- but that call\r\n 136:   sits inside a BARE `except Exception: pass`\r\n 137:   (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:626-636), so today a style-resolution failure there\r\n 138:   is silently swallowed. r1 must-fix: on the dynamic lane the style must be\r\n 139:   resolved BEFORE the beat loop, outside that fail-soft block (section 6.2).\r\n 140: - The helper family (`_resolve_style` :330, `get_era_tail` :344,\r\n 141:   `compose_still_prompt` :590, `finish_visual_prompt` :667 in\r\n 142:   nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py) resolves the pack from meta.\r\n 143:   render_driver reads pack `motion_registers`\r\n 144:   (nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_driver.py, visual_style reads).\r\n 145: - LOOK-AUTHORITY REALITY (r1 codex M3): the era tail is BRIEF-FIRST -- the\r\n 146:   brief's `atmosphere_line`/`visual_palette`/lighting win, and the pack's\r\n 147:   `era_tail` is only the fallback default\r\n 148:   (nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:356-370, 401, 414, 428). Any design that\r\n 149:   authors a new palette in the pack alone would be silently shadowed by the\r\n 150:   brief. Section 5.3 resolves the precedence for the dynamic lane.\r\n 151: - ShotLock stamps per-shot `creative` sidecars with `prompt_hash` +\r\n 152:   `request_hash` into `ledger['video'].shots[]`\r\n 153:   (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:637-647, 913-948).\r\n 154: \r\n 155: ### 1.6 Image dispatch, cache, and persistence (the replay substrate)\r\n 156: \r\n 157: - Dispatcher cache key: `request_cache_key(role, object_id, prompt_hash, seed,\r\n 158:   engine_id, engine_version, kind, w, h)` -- \"a change in ANY field -> new key\r\n 159:   -> regen\" (nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:117-129). Seeds:\r\n 160:   `resolve_object_seed` (request_hash mode; pinned bookend seed) (:132-162).\r\n 161: - Results land in `ledger[\"images\"] = {image_revision, images[], cache_index}`\r\n 162:   and are persisted to the DISK ledger via\r\n 163:   `stamp_durable(sections={\"images\": ...})`\r\n 164:   (nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:796-826;\r\n 165:   nodes/production_ledger.py:408-422).\r\n 166: \r\n 167: ### 1.7 Ledger save/merge ownership (what survives, what gets dropped)\r\n 168: \r\n 169: `Ledger.save()` merges in-memory state with the on-disk ledger\r\n 170: (BUG-LOCAL-108 lineage, nodes/production_ledger.py:1287-1346, 1357-1513):\r\n 171: \r\n 172: - TOP-LEVEL: only `TOP_PRESERVE = (schema_version, audio_gates, transitions,\r\n 173:   radio_bookend_path)` is copied forward from disk\r\n 174:   (nodes/production_ledger.py:1387-1393). An unknown top-level key present on\r\n 175:   disk but absent from a later in-memory save is DROPPED. Top-level is\r\n 176:   therefore NOT ledger-safe for a new artifact.\r\n 177: - META: per-key merge -- disk wins only where in-mem lacks the key or holds an\r\n 178:   empty value; in-mem wins where it has a real value\r\n 179:   (nodes/production_ledger.py:1403-1413). A namespaced meta key written once\r\n 180:   SURVIVES every later save by construction.\r\n 181: - ROWS (lines/clips/music): row-level ownership. `_MERGE_OWNED_ROW_FIELDS`\r\n 182:   (19 owned content/state fields) are never resurrected from disk\r\n 183:   (nodes/production_ledger.py:1441-1459); out-of-band DURABLE renderer fields\r\n 184:   copy forward only on a content-identity match\r\n 185:   (nodes/production_ledger.py:1477-1491, identity at :305-347). NOTE (r1): the\r\n 186:   merge boundary controls DISK COPY-FORWARD only -- it is not a runtime\r\n 187:   mutation validator; story-immutability protection comes from the projection\r\n 188:   comparison in section 6.3.\r\n 189: - The freeze audit hard-requires the fixed top-level list set and per-line\r\n 190:   shape (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:118-129, 252-404); it does not govern\r\n 191:   namespaced meta keys.\r\n 192: - Source-bank law, same conclusion from the docs side: \"Evidence maps and\r\n 193:   authorship receipts live in typed artifacts or namespaced `meta`; the fixed\r\n 194:   line schema contains no ad hoc provenance fields\"\r\n 195:   (docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:184-186). Freeze policy selection + receipts\r\n 196:   precedent: docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:187-194, 277-288.\r\n 197: \r\n 198: ---\r\n 199: \r\n 200: ## 2. Proposed typed artifact: `meta.visual_direction` (schema `vd-1`)\r\n 201: \r\n 202: One JSON object, stamped once per episode, versioned, hash-sealed. It contains\r\n 203: a synthesized visual-style pack (v2 schema) plus the evidence and receipts\r\n 204: around it, so every existing consumer keeps consuming a `VisualStyle` and never\r\n 205: learns a second prompt-composition path.\r\n 206: \r\n 207: ### 2.1 Shape\r\n 208: \r\n 209: ```json\r\n 210: {\r\n 211:   \"schema_version\": \"vd-1\",\r\n 212:   \"created_utc\": \"2026-07-12T00:00:00+00:00\",\r\n 213:   \"writer\": { \"node\": \"OTR_DynamicStoryDirection\", \"node_rev\": \"<git short>\" },\r\n 214: \r\n 215:   \"model_receipt\": {\r\n 216:     \"slot\": \"creative\",\r\n 217:     \"requested_model\": \"<the stable handle requested>\",\r\n 218:     \"resolved_model\": \"<provider-reported concrete model, when available>\",\r\n 219:     \"runtime_policy\": { \"...\": \"policy_from_meta snapshot\" },\r\n 220:     \"effective_sampling\": { \"temperature\": 0.1, \"do_sample\": true,\r\n 221:                             \"top_p\": \"<as configured>\", \"max_new_tokens\": 0 },\r\n 222:     \"attempts_used\": 1,\r\n 223:     \"prompt_sha256\": \"<sha256 of the full derivation prompt>\",\r\n 224:     \"response_sha256\": \"<sha256 of the raw accepted model output>\"\r\n 225:   },\r\n 226: \r\n 227:   \"story_binding\": {\r\n 228:     \"episode_id\": \"<ledger episode_id>\",\r\n 229:     \"freeze_verdict\": \"frozen_clean\",\r\n 230:     \"freeze_timestamp\": \"<meta.freeze_timestamp verbatim>\",\r\n 231:     \"story_projection_sha256\": \"<canonical sha256 of the PROJECTION, 2.3>\",\r\n 232:     \"content_mutations\": 0\r\n 233:   },\r\n 234: \r\n 235:   \"rationale\": {\r\n 236:     \"style_language\": \"<one-paragraph episode visual thesis>\",\r\n 237:     \"motifs\": [ { \"motif\": \"<recurring visual motif>\",\r\n 238:                   \"evidence\": [\"line:l0007\"] } ],\r\n 239:     \"clue_visual\": { \"treatment\": \"<how the clue mechanism reads on screen>\",\r\n 240:                      \"evidence\": [\"beat:b003\", \"line:l0012\"] },\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
