{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$start=241; $end=480; $i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r2\\\\input.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; if ($i -ge $start -and $i -le $end) { '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ } }'","aggregated_output":" 241:     \"era_cues\": [\"<cue>\", \"...\"],\r\n 242:     \"composition_notes\": [\"<non-executable note>\", \"...\"]\r\n 243:   },\r\n 244: \r\n 245:   \"style_pack\": {\r\n 246:     \"style_id\": \"dynamic_story\",\r\n 247:     \"schema_version\": \"v2\",\r\n 248:     \"...\": \"the COMPLETE v2 field set -- assembled per 2.2 from the vetted\r\n 249:             safety base + the LLM-authored look whitelist -- validated by the\r\n 250:             SAME _validate_row rules (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:184+)\"\r\n 251:   },\r\n 252:   \"authored_fields\": [\"era_tail\", \"positive_tail\", \"...\"],\r\n 253:   \"field_evidence\": {\r\n 254:     \"/style_pack/era_tail\": { \"evidence\": [\"line:l0003\", \"meta:episode_title\"],\r\n 255:                               \"kind\": \"factual\" },\r\n 256:     \"/style_pack/portrait_look\": { \"evidence\": [\"cast:c01\", \"beat:b002\"],\r\n 257:                                    \"kind\": \"factual\" },\r\n 258:     \"/rationale/style_language\": { \"evidence\": [\"title\"],\r\n 259:                                    \"kind\": \"rationale\" }\r\n 260:   },\r\n 261: \r\n 262:   \"shots\": [\r\n 263:     { \"beat_id\": \"<line_id>\",\r\n 264:       \"subject_note\": \"<what this beat's still should feature, <=240 chars>\",\r\n 265:       \"mood\": \"<one register word>\",\r\n 266:       \"evidence\": [\"line:<line_id>\"] }\r\n 267:   ],\r\n 268: \r\n 269:   \"semantic_sha256\": \"<canonical sha256 over style_pack + authored_fields +\r\n 270:                       field_evidence + shots + rationale + story_binding\r\n 271:                       (timestamps and model_receipt EXCLUDED)>\",\r\n 272:   \"artifact_sha256\": \"<canonical sha256 of the whole object minus this field>\"\r\n 273: }\r\n 274: ```\r\n 275: \r\n 276: Hash discipline (r1 codex M6): `semantic_sha256` covers only authored content\r\n 277: and its binding -- NO timestamps, NO model receipt -- so \"same story, same\r\n 278: direction\" is checkable across runs; `artifact_sha256` seals the full envelope\r\n 279: for corruption detection. `created_utc` never contaminates the semantic hash.\r\n 280: \r\n 281: ### 2.2 Who authors which pack field (r1 codex M4 -- the safety split)\r\n 282: \r\n 283: The LLM does NOT author the full v2 pack. The pack is ASSEMBLED from two\r\n 284: sources and then validated whole:\r\n 285: \r\n 286: - **Vetted safety base (checked-in, operator-owned; not LLM-touched):**\r\n 287:   `portrait_look_talking` (S4b lip-sync law -- bright/frontal/warm,\r\n 288:   nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:160-168), `announcer_subject_face`,\r\n 289:   `announcer_subject_ltx_mouth` (mouth-vocabulary contract,\r\n 290:   nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:117-119), `announcer_subject_object`,\r\n 291:   `open_subjects` ({form} templates), `motion_registers` (240-char engine\r\n 292:   budget, :121-123), `non_character_emblem_fallback`, `allow_radio_tails`,\r\n 293:   `forbidden_terms`.\r\n 294: - **LLM-authored look whitelist (the creative surface):** `label`,\r\n 295:   `era_tail`, `positive_tail`, `image_grade_tail`, `broadcast_tail`,\r\n 296:   `portrait_look`, `portrait_instruction_look`, `scene_instruction_look`,\r\n 297:   `radio_object_look`, `plate_look`, `still_word_title_mood_style`, and the\r\n 298:   VALUES of `still_word_typography` / `still_word_backdrop` (the genre\r\n 299:   SELECTOR stays Python-locked,\r\n 300:   nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:997-1002; the LLM authors the selected\r\n 301:   genre's row richly and fills the remaining fixed keys with the episode\r\n 302:   default row).\r\n 303: - `authored_fields` records exactly which fields the LLM wrote; everything\r\n 304:   else provably came from the safety base.\r\n 305: - The anti-geometry lint over authored fields uses a PYTHON-OWNED fixed\r\n 306:   vocabulary (framing/headroom/crop/close-up/mouth-visibility terms), never\r\n 307:   the artifact's own `forbidden_terms` (an LLM must not author its own guard).\r\n 308: \r\n 309: ### 2.3 The story projection (r1 codex M1 / antigravity M1 -- what gets hashed)\r\n 310: \r\n 311: Raw `lines`/`cast` mutate post-freeze by design (timing overlay,\r\n 312: nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:169-221; voice assignment,\r\n 313: nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:493-502). The binding therefore hashes an\r\n 314: IMMUTABLE AUTHORED-CONTENT PROJECTION -- exactly the fields the merge layer\r\n 315: already declares author-owned (nodes/production_ledger.py:1441-1448):\r\n 316: \r\n 317: | Array | Projected fields |\r\n 318: |---|---|\r\n 319: | lines | line_id, text, char_id, speaker_role, beat_id, traits, boundary, skip, tts_skip_reason |\r\n 320: | cast  | char_id, name, gender, traits, character_description |\r\n 321: | beats | beat_id, and its line-reference field(s) as shipped |\r\n 322: | meta (whitelist) | episode_title, style, source_bank, visual_style, story_brief_terms |\r\n 323: \r\n 324: `story_projection_sha256` = canonical sha256 (pattern:\r\n 325: nodes/production_ledger.py:292-302) over that projection. Writer and readers\r\n 326: compute it with ONE shared pure helper so the two sides can never drift.\r\n 327: Evidence VALUES cited in `field_evidence` resolve against the same projection,\r\n 328: so a cited line's text is covered by the hash.\r\n 329: \r\n 330: ### 2.4 Evidence ID grammar\r\n 331: \r\n 332: `line:<line_id>`, `beat:<beat_id>`, `cast:<char_id>`, `meta:<dotted.path\r\n 333: within the meta whitelist>`, `title`. Every ID must resolve against the bound\r\n 334: projection; an unresolvable ID is a validation error (fail-closed). Every\r\n 335: LLM-authored prompt-bearing field MUST have a `field_evidence` entry (keyed by\r\n 336: JSON pointer); entries are typed `factual` (cites story content) or\r\n 337: `rationale` (creative justification) -- ID existence proves traceability, the\r\n 338: `kind` split keeps the audit honest about what is derivation vs taste\r\n 339: (r1 codex M5). `shots[].beat_id` must match the ShotLock beat-id scheme\r\n 340: (line_id / synthetic `b000_music_open`; nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:279-296,\r\n 341: nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1016-1023).\r\n 342: \r\n 343: ### 2.5 Deliberately OUT of vd-1 (r1 cuts, judged)\r\n 344: \r\n 345: - `scenes[]` -- no canonical scene key exists on the visual wire; per-beat\r\n 346:   `shots[]` covers the intent. CUT.\r\n 347: - `global.continuity` -- `meta.continuity` already has one owner (the writer's\r\n 348:   continuity ledger, nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:4721-4746) and character\r\n 349:   look continuity is already carried by the cast rows the appearance lookup\r\n 350:   reads (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:116-153). The direction node CITES those as\r\n 351:   evidence; it never re-authors them. CUT.\r\n 352: - Wardrobe -- `OTR_OUTFIT_LOCK` stays the one wardrobe authority\r\n 353:   (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:143-153). Orthogonal. CUT (D7 resolved).\r\n 354: - Executable `composition_rules` -- geometry law; survives only as\r\n 355:   non-executable `rationale.composition_notes`. CUT as an authority.\r\n 356: - Reroll/revision machinery -- cut from v1 wholesale (section 6.5).\r\n 357: - Credits/dossier integration -- not part of the first build. CUT.\r\n 358: \r\n 359: `rationale.motifs` / `clue_visual` are KEPT (the operator product intent names\r\n 360: them) but they are NON-EXECUTABLE: nothing downstream composes prompts from\r\n 361: them; they exist as the evidence-bound reasoning that produced the pack tails.\r\n 362: \r\n 363: ---\r\n 364: \r\n 365: ## 3. Ownership: exactly one writer, read-only consumers\r\n 366: \r\n 367: | Actor | Role | Grounding |\r\n 368: |---|---|---|\r\n 369: | OTR_DynamicStoryDirection (NEW node -- not implemented) | SOLE writer of `meta.visual_direction`. Runs post-freeze, reads the frozen ledger read-only, stamps the artifact, forwards patched `script_json`. Pure pass-through when the sentinel is not selected. | Insertion at the FreezeCascade out[1] fan-out (links 255/252, section 1.4) |\r\n 370: | OTR_LedgerScriptWriter | Writes `meta.visual_style` only (now possibly the sentinel value). Never writes `visual_direction`. | nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3651-3655 |\r\n 371: | `resolve_visual_direction(ledger)` (NEW ledger-aware seam -- not implemented) | The ONE reader that validates the artifact against the ledger and returns the assembled `VisualStyle`. Called at each consumer ENTRY (which all hold the parsed ledger); `_resolve_style`/`get_visual_style` stay meta-only for named packs. | replaces the naive branch; see 4.3 |\r\n 372: | OTR_MetaBriefImagePromptGen | Consumer (portraits, scene stills, radio-host, mesh fodder, plates, still_word) + MANDATORY consumer of `shots[]` notes for beat stills on the dynamic lane. | nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1601-1609, 2134-2168 |\r\n 373: | OTR_ShotLock | Consumer; on the dynamic lane resolves the style BEFORE the beat loop, outside the fail-soft finisher block. | nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:626-636 (the block to hoist past) |\r\n 374: | render_driver | Consumer of pack `motion_registers` -- which on the dynamic lane come from the SAFETY BASE, so engine motion never varies with LLM output. | section 2.2 |\r\n 375: | OTR_ImageGenDispatcher | Indirect consumer: prompts arrive pre-composed; its cache key already reacts to any prompt change; it receives the artifact via ShotLock's whole-ledger re-serialization. | nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:117-129; nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1040, 1142 |\r\n 376: \r\n 377: ---\r\n 378: \r\n 379: ## 4. Lifecycle and storage decision (grounded, not guessed)\r\n 380: \r\n 381: ### 4.1 Location: `meta.visual_direction`. Nothing else is ledger-safe.\r\n 382: \r\n 383: - Top-level is ruled out by the merge code: only `TOP_PRESERVE` survives a\r\n 384:   later in-memory save (nodes/production_ledger.py:1387-1393); the freeze\r\n 385:   audit also pins the top-level shape (nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:118-129).\r\n 386: - Line/cast rows are ruled out by row ownership\r\n 387:   (nodes/production_ledger.py:1441-1459) and the preflight law\r\n 388:   (docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:184-186).\r\n 389: - META survives by construction: per-key merge keeps a real in-memory value\r\n 390:   and back-fills from disk when a later save lacks the key\r\n 391:   (nodes/production_ledger.py:1403-1413) -- exactly how `meta.visual_style`,\r\n 392:   `meta.freeze_*`, `meta.gap_audit_*` persist today.\r\n 393: \r\n 394: ### 4.2 Write path\r\n 395: \r\n 396: 1. Preconditions (ALL fail-closed): `meta.visual_style == \"dynamic_story\"`;\r\n 397:    `meta.cleanup_locked is True`; `meta.freeze_verdict` in\r\n 398:    `{frozen_clean, frozen_with_warns}` (`needs_full_rerun` refuses;\r\n 399:    nodes/_otr_ledger_freeze.py:787-811); non-empty `lines`/`cast`.\r\n 400: 2. Compute `story_projection_sha256` FIRST (section 2.3).\r\n 401: 3. Run the LLM derivation on the CREATIVE slot (recommended -- this is a taste\r\n 402:    task; final call is D2) via the existing seam\r\n 403:    (`request_slot`/`make_generate_fn` + `policy_from_meta`,\r\n 404:    nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:677-694), bounded attempts (2, matching\r\n 405:    `max_reseed`, nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:507); exhaustion fails closed\r\n 406:    (docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:132-133).\r\n 407: 4. Assemble the pack (safety base + authored whitelist, 2.2); validate vd-1 +\r\n 408:    the embedded pack + evidence resolution + the Python geometry lint.\r\n 409: 5. Re-compute the projection hash and refuse to stamp on any delta\r\n 410:    (`content_mutations: 0` receipt).\r\n 411: 6. Stamp `meta.visual_direction` on the wire ledger AND persist via\r\n 412:    `stamp_durable(meta_updates={\"visual_direction\": ...})`\r\n 413:    (nodes/production_ledger.py:408-422).\r\n 414: \r\n 415: ### 4.3 Read path (the r1-corrected seam)\r\n 416: \r\n 417: `get_visual_style(meta)` cannot enforce the staleness matrix -- it never sees\r\n 418: the arrays (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:378-390). The design therefore adds\r\n 419: ONE ledger-aware function, `resolve_visual_direction(ledger) -> VisualStyle`,\r\n 420: called at each consumer ENTRY, where the parsed ledger is already in hand:\r\n 421: `derive_image_prompts` receives `cast` + `lines` + `meta` from the node\r\n 422: (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:2134-2168), and ShotLock holds the whole\r\n 423: `led` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1040). The entry resolves ONCE and threads the\r\n 424: returned `VisualStyle` down the existing `style=` parameters -- the\r\n 425: resolve-once contract already in force (:1601-1609). REJECTED alternative\r\n 426: (r1): reading the `peek_ledger()` process singleton inside `get_visual_style`\r\n 427: -- consumers operate on the WIRE ledger, and the singleton can lag or be\r\n 428: absent in that seam.\r\n 429: \r\n 430: The dynamic `VisualStyle` instance NEVER enters the module pack cache\r\n 431: (`_STYLES`, nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:170, 355-359); it is built per\r\n 432: resolve from the artifact (r1 antigravity S3).\r\n 433: \r\n 434: ### 4.4 Look authority on the dynamic lane (r1 codex M3)\r\n 435: \r\n 436: Today the brief outranks the pack for the era tail\r\n 437: (nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:356-370, 401, 414, 428) -- correct for\r\n 438: named packs (the brief carries the episode's specifics), but on the dynamic\r\n 439: lane it would shadow exactly the palette the LLM just authored, leaving TWO\r\n 440: competing look authorities. Rule: **on the dynamic lane the artifact pack is\r\n 441: the SOLE final-look authority; the brief is evidence INPUT to the direction\r\n 442: LLM, not a runtime override.** Concretely: `get_era_tail` (and the palette\r\n 443: reads inside the still/portrait profiles) must, when the resolved style is\r\n 444: dynamic, return the pack-authored tail instead of the brief-derived one. The\r\n 445: derivation prompt receives the brief verbatim, so brief specifics reach the\r\n 446: final look THROUGH the authored pack, with evidence recorded.\r\n 447: \r\n 448: ### 4.5 VRAM handoff (r1 codex M8 / antigravity S1)\r\n 449: \r\n 450: The direction node reloads an LLM after the cascade deliberately unloaded it\r\n 451: (nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:377-387, 453-478). The node must mirror\r\n 452: that contract: `unload_llm_if_local_resident()` in a `finally`, a\r\n 453: `meta.visual_direction_unload_ok` stamp on failure, loud logging -- so image\r\n 454: dispatch never starts with a resident writer LLM on the 16 GB card. Lazy\r\n 455: imports throughout (module top level imports stdlib only -- the repo's\r\n 456: import-isolation posture; nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:11-13).\r\n 457: \r\n 458: ---\r\n 459: \r\n 460: ## 5. Dropdown / override semantics\r\n 461: \r\n 462: - The writer dropdown gains ONE entry: `dynamic_story`, appended CODE-SIDE as\r\n 463:   a sentinel next to `list_style_ids()` (the `ADD_CUSTOM` idiom,\r\n 464:   nodes/otr_video_director.py:35). The placeholder-pack-file alternative is\r\n 465:   REJECTED (r1): a renderable placeholder pack is a silent-fallback hazard.\r\n 466: - **Sentinel gate fix (r1 must-fix, was understated in rev 1):** the writer's\r\n 467:   run() gate `resolve_visual_style(visual_style)` raises on any id without a\r\n 468:   pack file (nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3334-3339) -- selecting\r\n 469:   `dynamic_story` today would kill the run BEFORE the story exists. The gate\r\n 470:   must special-case the sentinel (accept it without registry resolution); the\r\n 471:   stamp mechanics stay unchanged (:3651-3655).\r\n 472: - **Explicit named pack always wins, byte-identical:** when\r\n 473:   `meta.visual_style != \"dynamic_story\"`, the direction node is a pure\r\n 474:   pass-through and every resolver behaves exactly as today. Absent/empty\r\n 475:   `visual_style` keeps resolving to `sci_fi_radio`\r\n 476:   (nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:386-389).\r\n 477: - **The sentinel VALUE is the only trigger.** Artifact presence never\r\n 478:   activates dynamic styling -- a stale `meta.visual_direction` under a named\r\n 479:   pack is inert (r1 anchor B3).\r\n 480: - Precedence summary: (1) named pack -> current behavior, dynamic machinery\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$start=481; $end=717; $i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r2\\\\input.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; if ($i -ge $start -and $i -le $end) { '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ } }'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$start=481; $end=717; $i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'kibitz-runs\\\\2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual\\\\r2\\\\input.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; if ($i -ge $start -and $i -le $end) { '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ } }'","aggregated_output":" 481:   inert; (2) `dynamic_story` -> artifact mandatory, fail-closed; (3) nothing\r\n 482:   -> production default pack. No env override, no silent fallback between\r\n 483:   lanes.\r\n 484: \r\n 485: ---\r\n 486: \r\n 487: ## 6. Failure, stale data, replay, and audit behavior\r\n 488: \r\n 489: ### 6.1 Fail-closed matrix (enforced in `resolve_visual_direction(ledger)`)\r\n 490: \r\n 491: With `meta.visual_style == \"dynamic_story\"`, ANY of the following aborts the\r\n 492: episode loudly (named error, never a fallback to a named pack):\r\n 493: \r\n 494: - `meta.visual_direction` absent or not a dict.\r\n 495: - `schema_version` not in the known set (`vd-1`).\r\n 496: - `story_binding.freeze_timestamp != meta.freeze_timestamp` or episode_id\r\n 497:   mismatch (a re-frozen or foreign ledger).\r\n 498: - Recomputed `story_projection_sha256` (section 2.3) differs from the bound\r\n 499:   value -- authored story content changed after direction. (Projection, not\r\n 500:   raw arrays: post-freeze timing/voice mutations are EXPECTED and must not\r\n 501:   false-fail -- r1 must-fix.)\r\n 502: - `artifact_sha256` mismatch (corruption detection -- the digest lives inside\r\n 503:   the mutable ledger, so this is a checksum, not tamper-proofing).\r\n 504: - Embedded `style_pack` fails v2 validation, or an `authored_fields` entry\r\n 505:   names a safety-base field (the LLM wrote where it must not).\r\n 506: - Any evidence ID fails to resolve; any authored prompt-bearing field lacks a\r\n 507:   `field_evidence` entry.\r\n 508: \r\n 509: Postures mirrored from: nodes/otr_image_director.py:428-456,\r\n 510: nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:1053-1061, nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:367-375.\r\n 511: \r\n 512: ### 6.2 The ShotLock swallow (r1 must-fix)\r\n 513: \r\n 514: ShotLock's prompt finisher wraps `finish_visual_prompt` in a bare\r\n 515: `except Exception: pass` (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:626-636) -- on the dynamic\r\n 516: lane that would silently convert every 6.1 abort into an unstyled prompt. The\r\n 517: dynamic-lane contract: resolve the style ONCE, before the beat loop, OUTSIDE\r\n 518: any fail-soft block, and pass `style=` into the finisher.\r\n 519: `VisualStyleError` and vd-1 validation errors must propagate.\r\n 520: \r\n 521: ### 6.3 Story immutability\r\n 522: \r\n 523: Protection is the PROJECTION COMPARISON (write-time re-hash refusing to stamp\r\n 524: on delta, 4.2 step 5; read-time re-hash, 6.1) -- NOT the merge ownership\r\n 525: boundary, which only controls disk copy-forward\r\n 526: (nodes/production_ledger.py:1426-1459), and NOT the freeze audit, which has\r\n 527: already run. (r1 correction of rev 1's over-claim.)\r\n 528: \r\n 529: ### 6.4 Scene-by-scene drift prevention\r\n 530: \r\n 531: - ONE pack per episode; the resolve-once threading contract\r\n 532:   (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1601-1609) puts the SAME instance\r\n 533:   behind every prompt.\r\n 534: - `shots[].subject_note/mood` are ADDITIVE clauses appended at the same seam\r\n 535:   the beat mood token uses today\r\n 536:   (nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1004-1008); they can never replace\r\n 537:   pack-level fields, are capped at 240 chars, and are linted against the\r\n 538:   safety-base `forbidden_terms` + the Python geometry vocabulary at\r\n 539:   validation time.\r\n 540: - On the dynamic lane MetaBrief's consumption of `shots[]` is MANDATORY\r\n 541:   (an authored note that is never consumed is dead scope; a beat_id present\r\n 542:   in `shots[]` but absent from the ledger fails validation).\r\n 543: - Engine-safety continuity is structural: talking/mouth/motion/subject fields\r\n 544:   come from the vetted base (2.2), so no per-episode LLM output can degrade\r\n 545:   lip-sync or motion behavior.\r\n 546: \r\n 547: ### 6.5 Replay, reruns, and the reroll cut (r1 codex M6 / antigravity M4)\r\n 548: \r\n 549: - Reroll/revision machinery is CUT from v1. A ComfyUI re-queue re-executes the\r\n 550:   writer and cascade anyway (fresh story, fresh freeze), and a node whose\r\n 551:   inputs are unchanged is served from cache -- so \"re-roll just the\r\n 552:   direction\" has no state source in v1. When it returns post-v1, the lever is\r\n 553:   a mutating widget (`request_seed`-style) to force the cache miss, plus\r\n 554:   persisted-artifact reuse keyed on\r\n 555:   `story_projection_sha256 + prompt version + requested model`.\r\n 556: - Replay behavior that DOES hold in v1: an unchanged artifact composes\r\n 557:   byte-identical prompts -> dispatcher cache HITs; any artifact change flows\r\n 558:   into `prompt_hash` -> new cache keys -> regeneration\r\n 559:   (nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:117-129). Seed scheme untouched\r\n 560:   (:132-162).\r\n 561: - SHOULD (observability): stamp `semantic_sha256` (short form) onto the\r\n 562:   dispatcher's image rows' provenance so an asset links to the exact\r\n 563:   direction that authored its prompt even after a later re-direction\r\n 564:   (today's rows carry prompt/render identity only, :117-129, 796-826).\r\n 565: \r\n 566: ### 6.6 Debug/audit walk (\"why does this shot look like this?\")\r\n 567: \r\n 568: 1. Rendered asset -> `ledger['images'].images[]` row (or\r\n 569:    `ledger['video'].shots[].creative`) -> `prompt` + `prompt_hash`\r\n 570:    (nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:796-826;\r\n 571:    nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:940-947).\r\n 572: 2. Prompt tail vocabulary -> `style_pack` fields (verbatim in the artifact) +\r\n 573:    the per-beat `shots[]` note keyed by the same beat_id;\r\n 574:    `authored_fields` says whether the LLM or the safety base wrote each.\r\n 575: 3. Each authored field -> its `field_evidence` pointer entry -> the exact\r\n 576:    frozen projection content that motivated it (factual vs rationale typed).\r\n 577: 4. `model_receipt` gives requested + resolved model, slot, effective sampling\r\n 578:    (the local lane samples -- temp 0.1 floor, do_sample=True, no seed:\r\n 579:    nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:687-692 -- so \"attempts\", not \"reseeds\");\r\n 580:    `story_binding` proves which frozen story it derived from.\r\n 581: \r\n 582: Pixels -> prompt -> pack field -> evidence -> frozen story text.\r\n 583: \r\n 584: ---\r\n 585: \r\n 586: ## 7. Likely future code/workflow surfaces -- ALL \"not implemented\"\r\n 587: \r\n 588: 1. **NEW node `nodes/otr_dynamic_story_direction.py`\r\n 589:    (`OTR_DynamicStoryDirection`)** -- not implemented. Full ComfyUI node\r\n 590:    contract: `INPUT_TYPES` (`script_json` forceInput; optional `gate_in`),\r\n 591:    `RETURN_TYPES/RETURN_NAMES` (`patched_ledger_json`, `direction_report`,\r\n 592:    `done` -- the standard opaque ordering STRING, the CastLock/ShotLock\r\n 593:    idiom, nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:966-969), `FUNCTION`, `CATEGORY`,\r\n 594:    `VALIDATE_INPUTS`. Registration in the package init's `_NODE_MODULES` /\r\n 595:    class + display mappings (`__init__.py`). Lazy heavy imports; VRAM\r\n 596:    teardown per 4.5.\r\n 597: 2. **Workflow JSON delta (same change as the node code, CLAUDE.md\r\n 598:    section 0)** -- not implemented. THREE link records, not two: one NEW link\r\n 599:    FreezeCascade(62) out[1] -> Direction in[0], plus links 255/252 re-sourced\r\n 600:    from Direction out[0] to MetaBrief(89) in[0] and ShotLock(90) in[0];\r\n 601:    update both nodes' `inputs[].link` and the source nodes' `outputs[].links`\r\n 602:    fan-out lists + `last_node_id`/`last_link_id`. `widgets_values`\r\n 603:    append-only. Re-validate: OTR_WorkflowValidator + JSON round-trip +\r\n 604:    link/widget audit.\r\n 605: 3. **`nodes/_otr_visual_direction.py`** (pure/stdlib, lazy) -- not\r\n 606:    implemented. vd-1 schema validation, the story projection + canonical\r\n 607:    hashing helper (shared by writer and readers), evidence resolution,\r\n 608:    geometry lint, pack assembly from safety base + whitelist.\r\n 609: 4. **`nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py`** -- not implemented. Code-side sentinel\r\n 610:    exposure for the dropdown; `visual_style_from_payload(dict)` funneling\r\n 611:    through `_validate_row`; dynamic instances bypass `_STYLES`.\r\n 612: 5. **`nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py`** -- not implemented.\r\n 613:    `resolve_visual_direction(ledger)` entry seam + the dynamic-lane look\r\n 614:    precedence in `get_era_tail`/palette reads (4.4).\r\n 615: 6. **`nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py`** -- not implemented. Sentinel-aware\r\n 616:    dropdown + run() gate (5).\r\n 617: 7. **`nodes/otr_shot_lock.py`** -- not implemented. Hoist style resolution\r\n 618:    above the beat loop on the dynamic lane (6.2).\r\n 619: 8. **Vetted safety-base pack data** (checked-in, likely\r\n 620:    `nodes/visual_styles/_dynamic_safety_base.json` or a Python constant --\r\n 621:    Codex's call; if a JSON file lives in `visual_styles/` it must be excluded\r\n 622:    from the registry sweep, which currently rejects unexpected non-pack files,\r\n 623:    nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:329-336) -- not implemented.\r\n 624: \r\n 625: ---\r\n 626: \r\n 627: ## 8. Focused test + live-smoke plan (for Codex to implement)\r\n 628: \r\n 629: Unit (CPU, `OTR_TEST_MODE=1`, injected `llm_fn` -- the established pattern,\r\n 630: nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:499-528):\r\n 631: \r\n 632: 1. **Schema round-trip:** valid `vd-1` validates; each required field's\r\n 633:    absence fails named; embedded pack goes through `_validate_row` verbatim;\r\n 634:    an `authored_fields` entry naming a safety-base field fails.\r\n 635: 2. **Fail-closed matrix:** one test per row of 6.1 -- all raise; NONE fall\r\n 636:    back to a named pack.\r\n 637: 3. **Inert-path byte-identity, PARAMETERIZED over every registered pack +\r\n 638:    absent/default style** (not just sci_fi_radio): serialized ledger, composed\r\n 639:    prompts, prompt_hashes, and dispatcher request keys are byte-identical\r\n 640:    before vs after the feature. Boundaries defined at those four surfaces\r\n 641:    BEFORE any GPU-asset comparison.\r\n 642: 4. **Projection stability:** timing overlay\r\n 643:    (nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:169-221-style mutations) + voice-preset assignment\r\n 644:    do NOT change `story_projection_sha256`; a one-word text edit DOES.\r\n 645: 5. **Merge survival:** stamp, save from an in-memory ledger lacking the key,\r\n 646:    assert restoration (nodes/production_ledger.py:1403-1413; mirror of\r\n 647:    test_ledger_merge_ownership).\r\n 648: 6. **Story immutability:** a mutating fake `llm_fn` scenario is refused with\r\n 649:    `content_mutations != 0`.\r\n 650: 7. **Determinism of hashing:** same fixture + same injected output =>\r\n 651:    identical `semantic_sha256`; `created_utc` variation changes ONLY the\r\n 652:    envelope hash.\r\n 653: 8. **Drift + geometry guards:** shots[] note with an exclusion/geometry term\r\n 654:    fails; shots[] beat_id not in the ledger fails; all pack-level look tokens\r\n 655:    identical across beats.\r\n 656: 9. **ShotLock propagation:** with dynamic selected and a broken artifact, the\r\n 657:    ShotLock path RAISES (does not swallow) -- pins the 6.2 hoist.\r\n 658: 10. **Look-QA rubric fixtures (r1 codex should-fix):** a small multi-genre\r\n 659:     fixture set (noir / western / sci-fi story projections) with an operator\r\n 660:     rubric -- specificity, palette/medium coherence, recurring identity,\r\n 661:     talking-lane safety, measurable difference from the fixed-pack control.\r\n 662:     Schema validity alone does not prove the direction is any good.\r\n 663: \r\n 664: Suite discipline: full regression + Bug Bible after every code chunk\r\n 665: (CLAUDE.md section 3); Three-File Contract for any new bug class.\r\n 666: \r\n 667: Live smoke (5080, headless :8000, reset per CLAUDE.md section 4):\r\n 668: \r\n 669: 1. **Control leg:** 30-word episode, `visual_style=\"sci_fi_radio\"` -- prompts\r\n 670:    byte-match the pre-feature baseline.\r\n 671: 2. **Dynamic leg:** `visual_style=\"dynamic_story\"` -- artifact present on the\r\n 672:    disk ledger with receipts; VRAM returns to baseline after the direction\r\n 673:    stamp (the 4.5 teardown) BEFORE image dispatch; still prompts carry the\r\n 674:    authored vocabulary; assets at `otr\\episodes\\<ep>\\` (Test-Path),\r\n 675:    `obs_publish OK`.\r\n 676: 3. **Stale-evidence leg:** edit one frozen line's text on the wire copy ->\r\n 677:    dynamic resolve aborts loudly (6.1 in vivo).\r\n 678: 4. **Replay leg:** re-queue unchanged -> dispatcher reports cache HITs (6.5).\r\n 679: \r\n 680: ---\r\n 681: \r\n 682: ## 9. Unresolved decisions for Codex\r\n 683: \r\n 684: Resolved by r1 (no longer open): sentinel = code-side, no placeholder pack\r\n 685: (old D1); no reroll in v1 (old D4); wardrobe orthogonal (old D7); per-shot\r\n 686: notes artifact-side with mandatory MetaBrief consumption (old D3); talking\r\n 687: lane pinned to the safety base (old D6 -- strongest form adopted).\r\n 688: \r\n 689: Still open:\r\n 690: \r\n 691: - **D2 -- LLM slot.** Recommendation: `creative` (taste task; codex r1\r\n 692:   concurs). Alternative: `technical` for schema-heavy structured output.\r\n 693:   Whichever is chosen, the receipt records requested + resolved identity\r\n 694:   (virtual vs provider-resolved ids demonstrably differ on the OpenRouter and\r\n 695:   Google lanes).\r\n 696: - **D5 -- still_word typography scope.** Design says: Python keeps the genre\r\n 697:   SELECTOR; the LLM authors the selected genre's typography/backdrop VALUES\r\n 698:   and fills the other fixed keys with the default row (2.2). Confirm, or pin\r\n 699:   still_word entirely to the safety base for v1.\r\n 700: - **D8 -- size budgets.** Proposed: notes <= 240 chars (mirrors the motion\r\n 701:   budget, nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:121-123), `shots[]` <= one row per\r\n 702:   non-skipped line, total artifact <= 64 KB canonical, plus an output-token\r\n 703:   reservation sized from line count (docs/SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md:140-141).\r\n 704:   Confirm numbers.\r\n 705: - **D9 (new) -- safety-base packaging.** JSON file under `visual_styles/`\r\n 706:   (needs a registry-sweep exemption, nodes/_otr_visual_styles.py:329-336) vs\r\n 707:   a Python-side constant module. Codex's call at build time.\r\n 708: - **D10 (new) -- dynamic-lane era-tail mechanics.** 4.4 fixes the PRECEDENCE;\r\n 709:   the concrete seam (a style-aware branch inside `get_era_tail` vs a\r\n 710:   pack-flag the helper honors) is an implementation choice.\r\n 711: \r\n 712: ---\r\n 713: \r\n 714: END. Docs-only deliverable; no code, tests, prompts, registries, or\r\n 715: workflows/otr_canonical.json were touched. Codex owns everything in section 7.\r\n 716: r1 kibitz artifacts: kibitz-runs/2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual/r1/\r\n 717: (driver_anchor.md, codex.md, antigravity.md, judgment.md, final.md).\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
