{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$start=1; $end=170; $i=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs\\\\PROD_BUG_LOG.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$i++; if ($i -ge $start -and $i -le $end) { '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $_ } }'","aggregated_output":"   1: # Production Bug Log (staging pre-Bible)\r\n   2: \r\n   3: **Contract (operator, 2026-07-10):** Claude appends entries here AUTONOMOUSLY, but\r\n   4: ONLY for bugs that actually failed in a live/prod run (live render, headless lane,\r\n   5: soak, published episode). Dev/audit/review catches get fixed, never logged. NO entry\r\n   6: here touches the Bug Bible directly -- at ship time the operator triggers a BUG\r\n   7: FAN-OUT over this log, which promotes approved entries into the survival-guide\r\n   8: Bible in bulk under the Three-File Contract (YAML + README count + regression\r\n   9: test, one commit). Promoted entries get marked `PROMOTED <bible-id>`; rejected\r\n  10: ones get marked `REJECTED` and stay for the record. Append-only, newest last.\r\n  11: Running tests/bug_bible_regression.py after every code change stays automatic\r\n  12: and is unrelated to this log.\r\n  13: \r\n  14: Entry format:\r\n  15: \r\n  16: ```\r\n  17: ## PBUG-YYYYMMDD-NN -- short title\r\n  18: - surfaced: <which live run: smoke/soak/episode + date>\r\n  19: - symptom: <one line, what the operator/log saw>\r\n  20: - root cause: <one line>\r\n  21: - fix: <commit sha + one line>\r\n  22: - verify idea: <candidate machine check for the future bible test>\r\n  23: - bible-worthy: <yes/no guess + why -- operator decides at fan-out>\r\n  24: - status: OPEN | PROMOTED <id> | REJECTED\r\n  25: ```\r\n  26: \r\n  27: ---\r\n  28: \r\n  29: Backfill note: entries PBUG-20260612-01 .. PBUG-20260711-02 were mined 2026-07-10/11\r\n  30: by a two-agent backsweep (git history + handoff/smoke docs), prod-only bar applied,\r\n  31: cross-checked against BUG_BIBLE.yaml (BUG-11.26 family, 12.47, 07.16 excluded as\r\n  32: already promoted). Confidence tags preserved from the sweep.\r\n  33: \r\n  34: ## PBUG-20260612-01 -- headless boot dies on cp1252 emoji print\r\n  35: - surfaced: detached headless soak/API boot, 2026-06-12\r\n  36: - symptom: boot dies ~13s, exit 1, \"SERVER DID NOT COME UP\"\r\n  37: - root cause: detached cmd inherits cp1252; prestartup_script.py printed U+2705/U+2713 -> UnicodeEncodeError\r\n  38: - fix: scripts/_otr_soak_server_launch.cmd sets PYTHONUTF8=1 + PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8; rule codified in CLAUDE.md section 5\r\n  39: - verify idea: launcher-path boot succeeds; any new boot path asserts UTF-8 env\r\n  40: - bible-worthy: yes -- Windows console-codec boot killer, hits any custom node that prints unicode at import\r\n  41: - confidence: MED (sourced from operating-rules doc, no dated incident log)\r\n  42: - status: PROMOTED BUG-02.15\r\n  43: \r\n  44: ## PBUG-20260616-01 -- LTX-AV soak VRAM peak 15.8GB over the 14.5GB cap\r\n  45: - surfaced: LTX full-episode soak, 2026-06-16 (976ab329)\r\n  46: - symptom: soak measured 15.8GB peak on a 14.5GB gate, both device modes\r\n  47: - root cause: Gemma text encoder stayed GPU-resident through the LTX pass\r\n  48: - fix: b0925c37 moved encoder to cpu; 1e5d66f4 REVERTED it after soak re-measure proved the offload ineffective -- record documents a fix attempt that live evidence disproved\r\n  49: - verify idea: full-episode soak VRAM peak check; assert S9 offload state matches the reverted decision\r\n  50: - bible-worthy: yes -- \"the obvious offload fix measurably did nothing\" is worth pinning so it isn't retried blind\r\n  51: - confidence: HIGH\r\n  52: - status: PROMOTED BUG-07.17\r\n  53: \r\n  54: ## PBUG-20260618-01 -- remote creative slot crashed episode with KeyError\r\n  55: - surfaced: live run with creative_model='openrouter:slot-a', 2026-06-18\r\n  56: - symptom: episode aborted at line-compose with KeyError\r\n  57: - root cause: resolve_creative_system_prompt did rows[repo_id] against a CURATED_LLM_MODELS-only dict; remote handles aren't in it\r\n  58: - fix: 1f196ac3 -- rows.get(repo_id) with MODERN-prompt default\r\n  59: - verify idea: full episode with a remote slot handle completes, modern prompt used\r\n  60: - bible-worthy: yes -- exact-match lookup vs non-curated id, recurring trap\r\n  61: - confidence: HIGH\r\n  62: - status: PROMOTED BUG-11.27\r\n  63: \r\n  64: ## PBUG-20260618-02 -- visualizer soak found 4-bug integration cluster\r\n  65: - surfaced: Task 2 visualizer soak, 2026-06-18 (4a92ed66, 21 clips)\r\n  66: - symptom: crashes/misbehavior on 0-frame beats, silent beats, missing master-audio slice, over-gated audio_ref\r\n  67: - root cause: four missing guards -- no 0-frame floor, no idle-scope handling, audio_ref wrongly gated in assert_usable, b000 master slice never fed\r\n  68: - fix: afab1a3 + c5c14c90 + d4607974 + bad1bba3\r\n  69: - verify idea: visualizer soak forcing silent/0-frame beats, status=success\r\n  70: - bible-worthy: yes -- soak-found cluster, four distinct root causes\r\n  71: - confidence: HIGH\r\n  72: - status: PROMOTED BUG-07.18\r\n  73: \r\n  74: ## PBUG-20260620-01 -- published episode bars overlay read the silent source\r\n  75: - surfaced: obs-final render pipeline, 2026-06-20 (8d7e6604 verification)\r\n  76: - symptom: bottom bars overlay baked flat/green instead of audio-reactive in a PUBLISHED episode\r\n  77: - root cause: bars overlay read the silent blend source instead of the master WAV\r\n  78: - fix: f6788882 -- bars read the master WAV\r\n  79: - verify idea: obs final render, assert bars track master audio amplitude\r\n  80: - bible-worthy: yes -- defect shipped to a published artifact\r\n  81: - confidence: HIGH\r\n  82: - status: PROMOTED BUG-08.07\r\n  83: \r\n  84: ## PBUG-20260622-01 -- UnboundLocalError crashed every episode at flag-stamp\r\n  85: - surfaced: night-soak window, 2026-06-22 (096ef64e)\r\n  86: - symptom: every episode crashed with UnboundLocalError at execution\r\n  87: - root cause: local `import os` inside run() made os function-local; the L2/L7 meta-stamp referenced os.environ before the local import line executed\r\n  88: - fix: 096ef64e -- local import at the stamp site; suite never exercised the heavy node so it slipped through\r\n  89: - verify idea: end-to-end test exercising the L2/L7 stamp; lint for mid-function shadowed imports\r\n  90: - bible-worthy: yes -- Python scoping trap invisible to unit tests\r\n  91: - confidence: HIGH\r\n  92: - status: PROMOTED BUG-05.10\r\n  93: \r\n  94: ## PBUG-20260622-02 -- announcer coerced to character role, voice engine crash\r\n  95: - surfaced: live-smoke, 2026-06-22 (ffe23245, \"(live-smoke)\" tag)\r\n  96: - symptom: pre-freeze sweep re-roled the announcer intro to character -> bark engine -> EngineUnusable\r\n  97: - root cause: cast_ids_from_ledger didn't exempt a cast row NAMED ANNOUNCER from role coercion\r\n  98: - fix: ffe23245 -- exclude ANNOUNCER-named rows from coercion\r\n  99: - verify idea: episode with announcer keyed as ordinary cast id renders clean\r\n 100: - bible-worthy: yes -- naming-convention trap in role coercion\r\n 101: - confidence: HIGH\r\n 102: - status: PROMOTED BUG-07.19\r\n 103: \r\n 104: ## PBUG-20260622-03 -- stage-direction-only character line crashed voice render\r\n 105: - surfaced: live-smoked fix set, 2026-06-22 (f8a8645e)\r\n 106: - symptom: a line with zero spoken content reached the voice engine and crashed the render\r\n 107: - root cause: no handling for a dialogue row that was pure stage direction\r\n 108: - fix: e62081f9 recompose to real dialogue (root); 9a4f0a71 silence backstop (NOTE: backstop is a fail-soft -- flag against current no-fallback law at fan-out)\r\n 109: - verify idea: force a stage-direction-only line through; assert recompose path, no crash\r\n 110: - bible-worthy: yes -- degenerate-content class\r\n 111: - confidence: MED\r\n 112: - status: PROMOTED BUG-07.20\r\n 113: \r\n 114: ## PBUG-20260623-01 -- refine-loop save failures racing the freeze cascade\r\n 115: - surfaced: live-smoke, 2026-06-23 (9f29f644)\r\n 116: - symptom: intermittent save failures during the refine loop\r\n 117: - root cause: loser-directory cleanup raced the freeze cascade\r\n 118: - fix: 9f29f644 -- ship the LAST revision, drop the racing cleanup\r\n 119: - verify idea: repeated refine-loop runs, zero save failures, freeze lands\r\n 120: - bible-worthy: yes -- race class, easy to reintroduce with future cleanup code\r\n 121: - confidence: HIGH\r\n 122: - status: PROMOTED BUG-12.48\r\n 123: \r\n 124: ## PBUG-20260702-01 -- night-queue proof9c: VRAM ceiling breach, zero clips\r\n 125: - surfaced: overnight night-queue run, 2026-07-02 (4dd79dbe verdict)\r\n 126: - symptom: leg produced zero clips; VRAM ceiling ops breach mid-run\r\n 127: - root cause: never fully isolated; retried at 832x448 per the verdict\r\n 128: - fix: none identified (diagnostic verdict only)\r\n 129: - verify idea: n/a until root-caused\r\n 130: - bible-worthy: no -- unresolved diagnostic, keep for the record\r\n 131: - confidence: LOW\r\n 132: - status: OPEN\r\n 133: \r\n 134: ## PBUG-20260703-01 -- overnight soak died: Ollama daemon down\r\n 135: - surfaced: overnight model-matrix soak, 2026-07-03 (c36dfe3e)\r\n 136: - symptom: soak died mid-run, local-LLM legs had nothing to call\r\n 137: - root cause: daemon down; no preflight health check in the soak launcher\r\n 138: - fix: c36dfe3e -- daemon started, soak relaunched (env fix, not code)\r\n 139: - verify idea: soak launcher preflights daemon health before queuing legs\r\n 140: - bible-worthy: maybe -- precondition-check class, though root cause was environmental\r\n 141: - confidence: HIGH\r\n 142: - status: OPEN\r\n 143: \r\n 144: ## PBUG-20260704-01 -- Sonilo cloud music rejected 422 provider_rejected\r\n 145: - surfaced: live cloud-audio proving run, 2026-07-04 (8f146394 \"F