tory-REVISION loop (v1, 2026-06-23)\r\n 3324:         is delegated to ``_refine_loop`` on the INITIAL call; each refine pass\r\n 3325:         re-enters this body with ``_refine_active=True`` and runs it directly.\"\"\"\r\n 3326:         # Stage 2C run-intent gate -- the FIRST statement of the body, before\r\n 3327:         # the story-scaffold env mutation, the refine gate, the budget resets,\r\n 3328:         # and _resolve_inputs (RSS fetch): a non-runnable source_bank pick\r\n 3329:         # fails ONCE, LOUD and CHEAP, with zero side effects. bank.runnable is\r\n 3330:         # the ONLY runtime gate; unknown id = UnknownBankError (no fallback).\r\n 3331:         # Chunk 3: the returned bank row is BOUND -- D.2.5 resolves the\r\n 3332:         # bank's interpreter contract from it (r2 codex M1).\r\n 3333:         _source_bank_row = _otr_story_routing.require_runnable_bank(source_bank)\r\n 3334:         # Stage 3C visual-style gate -- beside the bank gate, same zero-side-\r\n 3335:         # effect contract: an unknown visual_style id raises\r\n 3336:         # UnknownVisualStyleError here, before ANY story work (no fallback).\r\n 3337:         # Every REGISTERED style is valid to run (styles are prompt-tail\r\n 3338:         # deltas; no execution lane to gate).\r\n 3339:         _otr_visual_styles.resolve_visual_style(visual_style)\r\n 3340:         # scifi_fable2 S1b entry gates (r3/M4): the lane's word-budget gate\r\n 3341:         # runs HERE -- before the story-scaffold env mutation, the refine\r\n 3342:         # gate, the budget resets, and _resolve_inputs (the RSS fetch) --\r\n 3343:         # so an unsupported target_words fails ONCE, loud and cheap, with\r\n 3344:         # zero side effects. Keyed on the BANK's declared pipeline (not the\r\n 3345:         # bank id) so a future fable2-family bank inherits the gate. The\r\n 3346:         # runner re-asserts defensively at its own entry. The refine loop\r\n 3347:         # is unsupported on this lane S1-S3 (WriterTailContext law) -- a\r\n 3348:         # non-Off refine widget fails loud here too.\r\n 3349:         _selected_pipeline_id = str(getattr(\r\n 3350:             _source_bank_row, \"default_story_pipeline\", \"\") or \"\")\r\n 3351:         if _selected_pipeline_id == \"fable2_multipass\":\r\n 3352:             try:\r\n 3353:                 from . import _otr_scifi_fable2 as _F2GATE\r\n 3354:             except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- flat/standalone load\r\n 3355:                 import _otr_scifi_fable2 as _F2GATE  # type: ignore\r\n 3356:             _F2GATE.assert_supported_target_words(int(target_words))\r\n 3357:         if (_selected_pipeline_id in _RUNNER_BY_PIPELINE\r\n 3358:                 and (_refine_active or refine_target_grade != \"Off\")):\r\n 3359:             raise RuntimeError(\r\n 3360:                 \"[OTR_LedgerScriptWriter] dispatched custom pipeline \"\r\n===== 3635-3670 =====\r\n 3635:         meta[\"source_ref\"] = resolved[\"source_ref\"]\r\n 3636:         meta[\"source_meta\"] = dict(resolved[\"source_meta\"])\r\n 3637:         meta[\"source_rights\"] = dict(resolved[\"source_rights\"])\r\n 3638:         # kibitz r2-r4 provenance: any bank whose defaults define\r\n 3639:         # credits_source_line gets it stamped (data-driven -- the\r\n 3640:         # original_radio row always defines it, so its credits line is\r\n 3641:         # UNCONDITIONAL for that lane; science defines none and stays\r\n 3642:         # byte-identical). The credits roll renders the stamp when\r\n 3643:         # present -- no bank branch in the credits code.\r\n 3644:         _credits_line = str(\r\n 3645:             (_source_bank_row.defaults or {}).get(\"credits_source_line\")\r\n 3646:             or \"\"\r\n 3647:         )\r\n 3648:         if _credits_line:\r\n 3649:             meta[\"credits_source_line\"] = _credits_line\r\n 3650:         meta[\"story_scaffold\"] = _scaffold\r\n 3651:         # Stage 3C: stamp the visual style -- THE threading channel: every\r\n 3652:         # downstream visual composer reads meta[\"visual_style\"] via\r\n 3653:         # get_visual_style(meta) off the serialized ledger (stamp precedes\r\n 3654:         # all of them by construction -- verified 2026-07-05).\r\n 3655:         meta[\"visual_style\"] = resolved[\"visual_style\"]\r\n 3656:         # Story-quality v2 is BAKED IN (operator 2026-06-28): the dialogue-craft\r\n 3657:         # spine (objective gate, body-gate text-score, cliche span-repair,\r\n 3658:         # one-breath budget cap, news-coda bridge, two-principal scan + telemetry)\r\n 3659:         # IS the engine, not an opt-in lever. Always enabled -- the\r\n 3660:         # OTR_STORY_QUALITY_V2 env kill-switch is removed so the improvement can\r\n 3661:         # never silently regress. (Default was already True since 2026-06-23.)\r\n 3662:         meta[\"story_quality_v2_enabled\"] = True\r\n 3663: \r\n 3664:         # Ledger durability P1 (2026-05-19): persist a skeleton ledger to\r\n 3665:         # disk NOW, before the style-picker / news-interpreter / cast /\r\n 3666:         # outline LLM phases run. Those phases are several minutes and the\r\n 3667:         # most failure-prone part of the writer; pre-fix the first\r\n 3668:         # led.save() was not until the Phase 2B outline stamp far below,\r\n 3669:         # so a crash in any earlier phase left zero ledger on disk for the\r\n 3670:         # run. The skeleton is a valid sparse ledger (episode_id, meta\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
