diversity is the point, correctness comes from the\r\n 137:   grounding step.\r\n 138: - **UNTIL 2026-07-21 (operator directive 2026-07-09): ALSO seat `tencent/hy3:free` on every\r\n 139:   panel** -- Tencent Hy3, 295B MoE (21B active), 262K ctx, $0/$0 on OpenRouter, listing expires\r\n 140:   July 21 2026. Pass it via `--models` (skill panel.config.json is a read-only cache). Free =\r\n 141:   no budget impact; a 4th genuinely different family, strongest on ideas/R1 rounds. Uses a\r\n 142:   configurable reasoning effort like the other reasoning panelists. REMOVE this line after\r\n 143:   2026-07-21 or when the slug 404s.\r\n 144: - **Cowork (Claude) is ALWAYS a code-aware grounded PANELIST *and* the sole judge.** Write your\r\n 145:   own grounded review FIRST (every claim checked against the real Windows files via Desktop\r\n 146:   Commander, never the lagging Linux mount), THEN ground the panel's reviews, discard the\r\n 147:   misreads, and synthesize. The panel proposes; Claude disposes -- never outsource synthesis.\r\n 148: - **Four-round campaign, in order:** R1 high-level arc / creative approach -> R2 coding plan ->\r\n 149:   R3 wiring (workflow JSON / nodes / widgets + any re-baseline procedure) -> R4 final\r\n 150:   convergence (confirm no new must-fix). Re-loop a round only if it surfaces new material; stop\r\n 151:   at convergence (don't grind passes to hear \"looks good\" in more accents).\r\n 152: - **Never dry-run, never pre-compute the cost -- just spend and run it LIVE,** then state the\r\n 153:   actual spend after. (Only backstop = the global >= $20-or-irreversible gate, which roundtable\r\n 154:   passes never reach in practice.)\r\n 155: - **ARC ROUTING (operator directive 2026-07-09): R1 (ideas/high-level) = cloud `/roundtable`\r\n 156:   on the highest frontier models (that's where paid diversity earns its keep); R2-R4 (coding /\r\n 157:   wiring / convergence) = `/kibitz` (local Codex + Antigravity) ALWAYS PREFERRED -- $0, file-\r\n 158:   grounded. R1 via kibitz is also fine when economy matters. OpenRouter is paid except\r\n 159:   `tencent/hy3:free` (until 2026-07-21), so default mechanical review to the local panel.\r\n 160: - Artifacts under `docs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<topic>/roundtable/` (pass00..passNN_plan.md +\r\n 161:   passNN_judgment.md), UTF-8 no BOM, ASCII where practical.\r\n 162: ## 9. MODEL ROUTING -- when to spend Fable (operator directive 2026-07-03)\r\n 163: Fable is a scalpel, not a default. Spawn it ONLY when output quality depends on narrative\r\n 164: judgment; keep everything mechanical off it. This is about WHICH MODEL a subagent runs --\r\n 165: orthogonal to the filesystem rule in section 1 and the frontier roundtable panel in section 8\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
