{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$p='\"'C:\\\\Users\\\\jeffr\\\\AppData\\\\Roaming\\\\Claude\\\\local-agent-mode-sessions\\\\6503cb4a-a0ec-4e89-b422-c889f09084d6\\\\cff774c2-bb97-4b73-b186-daa560353c46\\\\local_c3e04439-19fe-4882-b9a7-855ceb95b189\\\\outputs\\\\otr_review_profile.md'; if(Test-Path -LiteralPath \"'$p){ Get-Content -Raw -LiteralPath $p } else { Write-Output '\"'MISSING' }\"","aggregated_output":"## MANDATORY EXTRA REVIEW INPUT (OTR dynamic-story-visual campaign)\n\nBefore you review the document, READ these files in the repo yourself:\n\n- `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md` -- the project's hard-won sprint lessons.\n- `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` -- operator directives; they win over any doc.\n- `docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md` -- the live-failure log (note PBUG-20260712-02 and\n  PBUG-20260712-03: a local model nested a valid declared collection at the\n  WRONG DEPTH inside caller rows, typed repair reproduced the nesting, and the\n  run failed closed. This is the dominant structured-output failure class here).\n\nGRADE the document under review against `docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md`.\nAn unmet lesson IS a finding -- report it as one, with the lesson number.\nPay particular attention to:\n\n- Lesson 1: is the ownership table complete? Is every field authored, derived,\n  or measured? Are the exact nested-row field lists stated as closed sets?\n- Lesson 2: does the design keep all FIVE representations in lockstep (base\n  prompt, typed schema, worked fixture, parser/validator, repair prompt)?\n- Lessons 3-4: is there a bounded typed-repair ladder designed BY FAILURE CLASS,\n  and is the authored-vs-mechanical repair line drawn correctly?\n- Lesson 5: are the context and output budgets sized from the REAL drivers\n  (line count, evidence rows, schema overhead, repair envelope) rather than\n  target_words? Is the true context cap for the selected model resolved, and\n  does the design fail LOUD when a provenance-sensitive prompt cannot fit?\n- Lesson 6: is there a model-diversity qualification ladder (two local families\n  plus one cloud creative lane, 30w then 120w) for the new LLM pass?\n- Lesson 7: is the canonical-workflow delta exact (link records, node entry,\n  widgets_values, output-link fan-out lists, validator audit)?\n- Lesson 9: is there a PROD_BUG_LOG expectation for live-smoke failures?\n- Sprint receipt: does the plan end with the receipt fields this feature fills?\n\nHARD BOUNDARY: this is a DOCS-ONLY design review. Do NOT propose that the\nreviewer edit code. Report findings with `file:line` grounding from the real\nrepo. Unsupported claims will be discarded by the judge.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$ranges=@(@(120,155),@(175,205),@(265,295)); $content=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs\\\\SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md'; foreach(\"'$range in $ranges){ Write-Output \"===== $($range[0])-$($range[1]) =====\"; for($n=$range[0];$n -le $range[1];$n++){ '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$content[$n-1] } }'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$ranges=@(@(120,155),@(175,205),@(265,295)); $content=Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs\\\\SOURCE_BANK_PREFLIGHT.md'; foreach(\"'$range in $ranges){ Write-Output \"===== $($range[0])-$($range[1]) =====\"; for($n=$range[0];$n -le $range[1];$n++){ '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$content[$n-1] } }'","aggregated_output":"===== 120-155 =====\r\n 120: - [ ] **Hard:** Every input-list-to-output-row transformation declares and\r\n 121:   tests exact ownership: one row per input item, one singular owned value per\r\n 122:   row, and complete downstream reference coverage. Base and repair prompts\r\n 123:   forbid numbered, secondary/tertiary, and suffixed pseudo-fields; Python\r\n 124:   validates the cross-artifact multiset and closure.\r\n 125: - [ ] **Hard:** Every canonical spoken line is traceable to an accepted model\r\n 126:   artifact. Parser extraction may remove declared serialization delimiters\r\n 127:   but does not rewrite the content field.\r\n 128: - [ ] **Hard:** Python creates only mechanical data such as IDs, order,\r\n 129:   references, enums, counts, hashes, and validated routing metadata. It does\r\n 130:   not create or alter spoken prose; mechanical serialization of already\r\n 131:   accepted verbatim rows is allowed.\r\n 132: - [ ] **Hard:** Invalid creative content returns to a model through a bounded\r\n 133:   repair. Exhaustion fails closed; there is no canned story fallback.\r\n 134: - [ ] **Hard:** Every rejection names the item, evidence, defect, and allowed\r\n 135:   correction. A model reviewer cannot create a fatal finding that\r\n 136:   deterministic code cannot corroborate.\r\n 137: - [ ] **Hard:** Base, structural-retry, and typed-repair prompts fit the\r\n 138:   resolved context cap of their actual slot/model. Provenance-sensitive calls\r\n 139:   fail loudly rather than truncate.\r\n 140: - [ ] **Hard:** Output reservations scale from the artifact's real size driver\r\n 141:   such as line count or evidence count, not only `target_words`.\r\n 142: - [ ] **Hard:** Models are never asked to calculate, report, or enforce exact\r\n 143:   word, line, item, or coverage counts. Python measures them\r\n 144:   deterministically and supplies measured defects to any creative repair.\r\n 145:   No model-produced or unused count field can gate production.\r\n 146: - [ ] **Hard:** Creative randomness uses OS entropy. Reproducibility comes\r\n 147:   only from the existing explicit seed overrides; the bank does not plant a\r\n 148:   fixed seed.\r\n 149: - [ ] **Hard:** `target_words` is advisory and recorded. It does not trigger\r\n 150:   deterministic trim, padding, culling, rewriting, or a fatal quota gate.\r\n 151: \r\n 152: ## Gate 4 -- Ledger closure and delivery\r\n 153: \r\n 154: - [ ] **Hard:** The provided `Ledger` is the only ledger. The root\r\n 155:   `cast`, `lines`, `beats`, `scenes`, `shots`, `music`, and\r\n===== 175-205 =====\r\n 175: - [ ] **Hard:** Every non-skipped voiced row has non-empty canonical text.\r\n 176:   Music sentinels may have empty text without being skipped. Every row marked\r\n 177:   `skip=True` has empty text and a non-empty `tts_skip_reason`. Spoken\r\n 178:   text has no speaker label, stage direction, or whole-line quotation wrapper.\r\n 179: - [ ] **Hard:** Every voiced line `boundary` is `shot_start`,\r\n 180:   `beat_start`, or `continue`, and agrees with the actual shot/beat\r\n 181:   transition.\r\n 182: - [ ] **Hard:** Counts and hashes are stamped from final canonical content,\r\n 183:   after all accepted model repairs.\r\n 184: - [ ] **Hard:** Evidence maps and authorship receipts live in typed artifacts\r\n 185:   or namespaced `meta`; the fixed line schema contains no ad hoc provenance\r\n 186:   fields.\r\n 187: - [ ] **Hard:** The pack deliberately selects its live freeze policy: non-empty\r\n 188:   `line_composer_system` means `legacy_full`; absence means\r\n 189:   `content_owned_readonly`. A test proves the expected policy.\r\n 190: - [ ] **Hard:** A content-owned runner assigns valid character `tts_model`\r\n 191:   and `voice_preset` values that satisfy the declared reuse policy\r\n 192:   (unique when reuse is disabled). Its proof survives while the shared writer\r\n 193:   tail stamps fresh `text_for_tts` and canonical-text source hashes. A\r\n 194:   legacy lane proves the shared CastLock/readiness path owns delivery.\r\n 195: - [ ] **Hard:** The lane-defined return object exposes `outline_view.title`\r\n 196:   and `outline_view.premise`; an EpisodeCanon-compatible `canon` with\r\n 197:   title, premise, setting, time of day, and sound palette;\r\n 198:   `final_title_override`; and `run_story_spine`. An optional\r\n 199:   `tail_finalizer` implements `before_save` and `after_save`.\r\n 200: - [ ] **Hard:** The bank-owned closure test passes independently of the freeze\r\n 201:   audit. Freeze warnings alone are not proof of full\r\n 202:   scene/shot/beat/line/cast closure.\r\n 203: \r\n 204: ## Gate 5 -- Registry, runner, and canonical wiring\r\n 205: \r\n===== 265-295 =====\r\n 265:   and word-count receipts are present.\r\n 266: - [ ] **Hard:** The final episode is published to `otr/obs`, and the exact\r\n 267:   asset path exists on disk. A resident server or VRAM allocation is not proof\r\n 268:   of completion.\r\n 269: - [ ] **Hard:** No deliverable remains in a temporary directory, and no\r\n 270:   temporary probe or generated workflow is included in the change.\r\n 271: \r\n 272: If an automated review panel is used, follow the current `AGENTS.md` and\r\n 273: `CLAUDE.md` rules. Ground every finding in live code. Review may find\r\n 274: implementation defects after the design lock; it may not redesign the bank's\r\n 275: creative premise by consensus.\r\n 276: \r\n 277: ## Final receipt\r\n 278: \r\n 279: ```text\r\n 280: SOURCE BANK PREFLIGHT: PASS | FAIL\r\n 281: \r\n 282: bank:\r\n 283: story_model:\r\n 284: story_pipeline:\r\n 285: design_fingerprint:\r\n 286: design_fingerprint_path_sha256:\r\n 287: comparison_matrix_path_sha256:\r\n 288: completed_check_matrix_path_sha256:\r\n 289: target_derived_choices:\r\n 290: source_mode:\r\n 291: source_and_rights_evidence:\r\n 292: llm_slot_evidence:\r\n 293: authorship_evidence:\r\n 294: ledger_graph_test:\r\n 295: tail_handoff_test:\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
