{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"agent_message","text":"VERDICT: no — the LLM contract, repair ladder, context budget, consumer wiring, and live qualification are not implementable as specified.\n\nMUST-FIX BEFORE BUILD:\n\n1. [§2.1-2.4, §3, §7.3; Lessons 1-2] The document conflates the LLM response with the Python-assembled artifact. The shown `vd-1` contains ellipses, derived receipts/hashes, an open `runtime_policy`, and no closed types, bounds, optionality, or extra-key policy. Define separate strict `VisualDirectionDraftV1` and final `VisualDirectionArtifactVD1` models; Python must add the safety base, receipts, hashes, and derived fields. Supply all five synchronized representations: base prompt, typed schema, valid worked fixture, parser/full validator, and repair prompt. Every nested row must list its exact allowed fields and ownership. Reusing `structured_call` requires a Pydantic `BaseModel`, contradicting §7.3’s “stdlib” claim unless that restriction is removed. Grounding: kibitz-runs/2026-07-12-dynamic-story-visual/r2/input.md:207-307,365-375; docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:7-36; nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:42,551-563; docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:469-485.\n\n2. [§4.2, §6, §8; Lessons 3-4] “Bounded attempts (2, matching `max_reseed`)” is neither a failure-class ladder nor numerically correct: `max_reseed=2` executes up to three calls. Use `structured_call(..., max_attempts=3)` with a strict draft schema, semantic post-validator, and custom typed-repair factory. Define JSON-syntax retry, typed/wrong-depth repair, semantic repair, incomplete-repair retry, and terminal failure separately. A deterministic repair may relocate existing values only when the destination is unique, then must pass the complete schema and semantic validator; otherwise use typed model repair and fail closed. Persist an attempt journal containing rung, reason, prompt/response hashes, validator result, and model identity. Grounding: kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:401-408; nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:499-507,542-558; nodes/_otr_structured_call.py:617-635,668-823; docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:38-64.\n\n3. [§2.3-2.5, §4.4, §6.1] The direction input, evidence universe, and hashes are not in lockstep. The projection excludes `story_brief`, `visual_palette`, `key_objects`, and `atmosphere_line` even though §4.4 says the brief is supplied verbatim; it also says `meta.continuity` is cited although continuity is outside the evidence whitelist. “Exactly” matching merge-owned fields is false, and beat fields remain “as shipped” instead of a closed set. Define one `DirectionSourceV1` DTO; serialize that exact DTO into the prompt, hash it, and resolve all evidence only against it. Explicitly enumerate line/cast/beat/meta fields, ordering, null normalization, and omitted-field rationale. Grounding: kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:309-341,347-351,434-446; nodes/_otr_story_brief.py:841-860; nodes/production_ledger.py:865-893,1441-1459.\n\n4. [§2.1, §6.1] The semantic-hash preimage contradicts itself: it includes `story_binding`, which contains `freeze_timestamp`, while claiming timestamps are excluded. The read matrix does not recompute `semantic_sha256`, compare `freeze_verdict`, or require `content_mutations == 0`. List the semantic preimage key-for-key, exclude volatile fields explicitly, recompute both hashes on every read, and compare episode ID, freeze timestamp, freeze verdict, projection digest, and zero-mutation receipt. Grounding: kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:227-279,489-507.\n\n5. [§3, §4.3, §6.4, §7] MetaBrief cannot consume the artifact as described and is omitted from §7’s implementation surfaces. `generate()` owns the ledger but passes only `cast`, `meta`, and `lines`; `derive_image_prompts` has no ledger, resolved-style, or direction-note parameter and calls the meta-only resolver, so `dynamic_story` raises. The cited mood seam applies only to `still_word`; mesh, character-scene, plate, and ordinary scene branches have separate prompt paths. Add `nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py` explicitly, resolve from the full ledger once, and pass a validated style plus note index through every applicable branch before the final prompt hash. Grounding: nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:942-1008,1570-1609,1939-2084,2134-2168.\n\n6. [§2.4, §6.4, D8; Lesson 1] `shots[]` lacks an exact mapping invariant and overloads `beat_id` with a line-derived render key. Define a closed sparse mapping: zero or one row per non-skipped line, unique target ID, source-line order, exact row fields, and complete consumption of every supplied row. Use `line_id` or `target_id`; reserve `beat:` for actual ledger-beat evidence. Exclude synthetic `b000_music_open` from authored rows or derive its validation universe through the same pure helper MetaBrief uses, because it is absent when Direction runs and only created later. Grounding: kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:262-267,330-341,529-545,700-703; nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:260-296,1084-1090; nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:1016-1086.\n\n7. [§3, §4.3-4.4, §7] `render_driver` remains an unfixed dynamic consumer. It directly calls `get_visual_style(meta)`, then one branch calls `finish_visual_prompt` without the already-resolved style; both reject the sentinel. The same branch still uses `get_story_brief_ltx(meta)` as runtime prompt core, contradicting the rule that the brief is evidence input rather than dynamic look authority. Add `render_driver.py` to §7, resolve once in `run_real_episode`, thread the result through `build_request_from_shot` and ShotLock’s preflight, and define a dynamic-only prompt core while leaving named packs byte-identical. Grounding: nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_driver.py:1220-1248,2051-2083,2446-2491; nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:705-787; nodes/_otr_story_brief_helpers.py:135-170.\n\n8. [§4.2, D2, D8; Lesson 5] The model API and budget remain unresolved. Choose the slot and corresponding meta key; if the recommendation stands, specify `request_slot(\"creative\", meta[\"creative_writing_model\"], policy=policy_from_meta(meta))`. Define a GenerateFn-compatible test injection rather than ShotLock’s incompatible `callable(prompt)->str` shorthand. The direct `make_generate_fn` path does not enforce `context_cap`; `max_new_tokens=0`, a string `top_p`, and an unconfirmed 64-KB artifact are not valid budgets. Preflight base and worst-case repair calls against the selected entry’s true cap, size output from line/note/evidence counts plus schema and repair-envelope overhead, bound every string/list, and raise before generation rather than truncate. Grounding: kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:215-224,401-406,689-704; nodes/_otr_model_loader.py:790-824,940-948,1061-1135; docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:66-75; docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:388-405,439-455,479-485.\n\n9. [§4.5] The VRAM guarantee is false as written. [ASSUMPTION: a local model is selected.] Direction may unload, but MetaBrief immediately reloads the writer model and ShotLock independently uses it; neither unloads before returning, so Dispatcher can begin with an LLM resident. Define post-freeze LLM ownership and a teardown barrier—prefer `finally` teardown in every node after its last LLM call. Distinguish “no local model existed” from teardown failure, persist/re-serialize the receipt after teardown, and abort before GPU image work if unloading raises. Grounding: nodes/otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py:2087-2095,2158-2187; nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:651-697,1098-1146; nodes/_otr_model_loader.py:743-754; nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:452-492.\n\n10. [§5, §7.1-7.2; Lesson 7] The canonical workflow delta is not exact enough to apply safely. From the current graph, use the next free node/link IDs 96/284, add `[284,62,1,96,0,\"STRING\"]`, change links 252/255 to sources `[252,96,0,90,0,\"STRING\"]` and `[255,96,0,89,0,\"STRING\"]`, change Freeze fan-out to `[16,231,232,233,284]`, and give Direction out[0] `[252,255]`; set `last_node_id=96`, `last_link_id=284`. Specify the entire node record, exact method signature/types, order shift, properties, and `widgets_values=[]`. Also update the existing widget test that requires choices to equal the pack registry exactly; keep `list_style_ids()` registry-only and test registry-plus-one-sentinel at the Writer surface. Grounding: workflows/otr_canonical.json:1; tests/test_visual_style_widget_3c.py:53-71,84-119; tests/test_visual_styles_3b.py:73-88; AGENTS.md:12-28.\n\n11. [§8; Lessons 6-7] Qualification is incomplete. Add canonical 30-word dynamic legs for two distinct local model families plus one cloud/frontier creative lane, then repeat all three at 120 words before any 720-word qualification. Every leg must load `workflows/otr_canonical.json` and record concrete model, slot, prompt ID, repair counts, ledger path, episode asset, and published asset. Grounding: kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:667-678; docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:77-108; AGENTS.md:20-21.\n\n12. [§6.5, §8] The live replay leg cannot pass. Writer and FreezeCascade deliberately return time from `IS_CHANGED`, so a canonical requeue creates a fresh story/freeze/artifact rather than replaying an unchanged artifact. Move replay and stale-wire mutation to deterministic CPU/integration tests over a captured frozen ledger; do not introduce an ad-hoc workflow or test-only mutation node. Also narrow “any artifact change” to “any prompt-affecting change,” because Dispatcher keys prompt hashes, not rationale or receipt changes. Grounding: nodes/OTR_LedgerScriptWriter.py:3023-3028; nodes/OTR_LedgerFreezeCascade.py:269-272; nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:117-129; kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:547-560,676-678.\n\n13. [§8; Lesson 9; Sprint receipt] The plan lacks the required production closeout. State that every actual live-smoke failure gets an append-only `PROD_BUG_LOG` entry, while dev-only failures do not. Verify the final file under `otr/obs/`, not merely `obs_publish OK`, and append the full sprint receipt with workflow hash, focused/full/Bug-Bible results, model pairings, 30/120 receipts, ledger/asset paths, bug entries, and HEAD/origin. Grounding: docs/PRODUCTION_SPRINT_LESSONS.md:120-165; docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md:1-24; AGENTS.md:120-142.\n\nSHOULD-FIX:\n\n1. [§2.1, §6.6] Make receipts provider-truthful. Separate requested from effective sampling and allow unknown values to be null: local generation hardcodes `do_sample=True` and `top_p=0.92`, while remote backends may override temperature and floor/clamp output tokens. Define backend-specific resolved-model and sampling extraction. Grounding: nodes/_otr_model_loader.py:1072-1128; nodes/_otr_openrouter_backend.py:958-985.\n\n2. [§2.1] Use a strict JSON-only canonicalizer for provenance seals. The cited helper falls back to `repr()` and never raises, which is inappropriate for a fail-closed artifact. Reject non-JSON values, NaN, infinity, and non-string object keys. Grounding: nodes/production_ledger.py:292-302.\n\n3. [§8.5] Split the merge-survival test. `OTR_TEST_MODE=1` makes `stamp_durable` skip disk writes, so test in-memory stamping separately from an isolated temporary-directory `Ledger.save()` merge, and test production failure when `save()` returns `None`. Grounding: nodes/production_ledger.py:408-452; kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:627-647.\n\n4. [§6.5-6.6] Make `visual_direction_semantic_sha256` required provenance on affected image rows and video creative sidecars if the stated historical audit walk must survive a later direction replacement. Current rows retain prompt/render identity only. Grounding: nodes/otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py:796-826; nodes/otr_shot_lock.py:637-647,940-947.\n\n5. [§8.3] Capture pre-feature named-pack prompt, hash, and request-key fixtures before implementation. Otherwise “before versus after” byte identity has no immutable baseline once the code changes. Grounding: kibitz-runs/.../r2/input.md:637-641,669-670.\n\n6. [§4.2] [ASSUMPTION: the node may be invoked directly or after stale process state.] Verify `peek_ledger()` exists and its episode ID matches the wire ledger before `stamp_durable`; that helper otherwise creates/updates the process singleton independently of the wire object. Grounding: nodes/production_ledger.py:372-397,408-444.\n\nOPTIONAL / NICE-TO-HAVE:\n\n- [§6.5] Add a direction-only reroll later, after defining an explicit seed/cache-invalidating input and persisted-artifact reuse key.\n- [§8.10] Retain the operator visual-quality rubric; automated similarity metrics are optional and must not replace visual review.\n\nCUT THESE (over-engineering):\n\n1. [§7.1-7.2] Cut unwired `gate_in`, `done`, and `direction_report` outputs for v1. The `script_json` edge already orders the node, and no declared consumer uses the extras.\n\n2. [D9] Cut the safety-base JSON packaging fork. Keep the vetted base as a Python constant beside assembly/validation; this avoids a registry exemption and external-file cache dependency.\n\n3. [D5] Cut dynamic typography/backdrop authorship for v1 and pin both maps to the safety base. It is unresolved, nonessential to the core feature, and otherwise forces the model to emit unused fixed-key rows.\n\n4. [§2.5] Cut `rationale.composition_notes`. It is explicitly non-executable while geometry remains Python-owned, so it only consumes schema and context budget.\n\n5. [§2.1-2.2] Cut `authored_fields` and `content_mutations` if the whitelist is fixed and stamping is refused on any mutation. Exact evidence-pointer equality plus the ownership table carries the same proof without redundant drift-prone fields.\n\n6. [§8] Cut any test-only workflow mutation or replay node. The same invariants are cheaper and valid at the pure resolver/cache seams without violating the canonical-workflow rule."}}
